*** merge_relate.pgm — Epiora v1.1 Task 3 reference program.
*** RELATE one-to-many then FREQ: Nutrition1 has 3 patients keyed PatientID
*** ("1","2","3"); all 11 PatientVisits2 rows carry VisitPatientID "1", so a
*** MATCHING relate expands patient 1 to 11 rows and ALL adds the two
*** unmatched parents. MERGE writes into the destination table, so this
*** program runs on a scratch copy (@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb): duplicate
*** source keys in UPDATE and APPEND modes, then a key with no destination
*** match to pin inserts. Pins spec §15.2: RELATE one-to-many then FREQ,
*** MERGE with duplicate keys in update and append modes.
READ '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':Nutrition1
ROUTEOUT "@OUTPUT_HTML@" REPLACE
DISPLAY TABLES
LIST PatientID LastName FirstName Sex
RELATE PatientVisits2 PatientID::VisitPatientID
LIST PatientID VisitPatientID VisitSex HeightInches
FREQ PatientID
READ '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':Nutrition1
RELATE PatientVisits2 PatientID::VisitPatientID ALL
LIST PatientID VisitPatientID HeightInches
FREQ Sex
READ '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':Nutrition1
MERGE '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':PatientVisits2 PatientID::VisitPatientID UPDATE
READ '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':Nutrition1
LIST PatientID GlobalRecordId
MERGE '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':PatientVisits2 PatientID::VisitPatientID APPEND
READ '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':Nutrition1
FREQ PatientID
MERGE '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':PatientVisits2 GlobalRecordId::GlobalRecordId UPDATE
READ '@WORK_DIR@/Nutrition.mdb':Nutrition1
FREQ Sex
CLOSEOUT
QUIT
